WEBVTT

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.000
Ah... I'm getting hungry...

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.410
"She's screaming again..."

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.330
Hey, Mina... Mina...!

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:34.910
Mitsuo!

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.580
That hole was two meters deep--
your arm strength is insane.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.330
Never mind that! Why are you alive?!

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.870
Mina... Let's have the master pray for us.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.410
No!

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.370
What?

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:51.250
Under the Sea of Trees, there's a divine woman

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.790
who claims to be the reincarnation
of Asama-no-Okami.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:02.790
She's going to purify our sinful souls
and guide us to the next life.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.830
Next life...?

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.410
--Let's go see her and find out
what she's talking about.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.200
--No way!
--Let's go see her and find out
what she's talking about.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.330
And where's Mr. Matt? What did you do
to the old man who was with me?!

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:15.910
Oh, him... He's underground listening to
the master's words of wisdom right now.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.500
I can't deal with all this craziness!

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:56.000
"Episode 11: I Don't Fear Anaerobic Creatures"
Hey, Mina, don't tell me you're worried that
the master's a scary person or something?

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.580
Look, there's nothing to worry about. She has
a plump figure that makes people feel safe.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.910
Like Mito-<i>chan </i>and Matsuko.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.000
Actually, I think those two
have drastically different body types.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.660
Never mind that! I'm still in the middle of
being shocked that a zombie's talking to me!

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.120
This is getting cumbersome.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.040
Come on.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:19.410
You're always way too self-centered!

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.620
Help!

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.910
"Rumble rumble rumble"
"Rattle rattle rattle"
"Crackle! Crackle!"

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.700
"Rumble rumble rumble"
"Rattle rattle rattle"
"Crackle! Crackle!"
It's so loud...

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.950
This is really amusing...

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.160
Even though it's not useful
for anything in the future.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.540
"Boom boom boom boom boom"

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.450
"Boom boom boom boom boom"
I've never been asked to create
underground sounds before.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.250
Do all of you understand...

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:59.080
...the reason why you've been summoned here?

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.950
Yes.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.040
I have a question! Why the heck are we
able to breathe underground like this?!

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.830
Well, let's see...

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.910
Do you know about anaerobic creatures?

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.000
--It's what we call creatures that
don't require oxygen to reproduce

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.200
--Was this voice processed from Mr. Mato's, too?
--It's what we call creatures that
don't require oxygen to reproduce

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.700
--That's impressive...
--or die if oxygen is present.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:21.700
Your bodies have been recomposed
to have that disposition now.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.950
Under great spiritual power!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.080
If you were going to conclude your
explanation with some fluff like that,

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.000
you could've just said we have
spiritual bodies now.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.410
The scientific talk in the beginning
was completely unnecessary!

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:34.580
Now, cough up the karma of this life.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:40.410
I shall cleanse that karma and guide
your soul to a new vessel.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.950
What does that mean?

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.040
The Aokigahara Sea of Trees...

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:50.330
By extension, Mt. Fuji was recognized
by UNESCO as a World Heritage Site in 2013.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:55.580
Considered a sacred mountain since ancient
times, it has also been an object of worship.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.790
This was of course partly nature worship,

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:03.620
but there is also known
to be a path used by spirits.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.700
The lost souls of more than 100 people
who commit suicide each year

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.450
--Was the UNESCO passage necessary?
--at the Sea of Trees linger there,

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.000
and they say this will eventually
cause Mt. Fuji to explode.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.040
What? Who's saying that?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.120
Can't you just shut your mouth?

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.040
On the occult boards, of course.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.370
Now, cough up the karma you possess.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.540
Let's start with the man on my left.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.830
Hey! Hey! Old lady! What the heck is a karma?

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:30.830
Oh, you really need to shut your mouth.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.830
Your weaknesses... things like that.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:39.500
So far... I've killed 19 people.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.120
I have an architecture firm as a front--

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.830
I've never used the office for anything
besides cleaning up dead bodies.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:49.000
I made an effort to live as a salaried man,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.790
but no matter what, I couldn't manage
to cooperate with those I despised.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:57.750
I can't stand being expected to have
some lame thing like communication skills.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.620
I'm the quintessential misfit, as they say.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:06.200
The worst of it all is that I had a friend who
was connected to the underside of society.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.500
I'll never forget my first kill...

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.750
It was 20 years ago in January...

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.660
I ran over and killed an executive
of a certain company

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.330
along with his granddaughter in the snow.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:23.040
After I drove away onto
a secluded woodland path...

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.660
Before I got out of the car...

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.580
...I vomited on the seat.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.660
If I had chosen to turn away from
the underground world,

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.620
that would've been the moment...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.870
But I couldn't manage to do it, after all.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.080
So for the next 20 years,
I continued to kill people.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.700
I have no regrets.
What do I have to regret, anyway?

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:44.910
When there was only one path I was able to take.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.120
But if I were able to be something else...

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.200
I would want to be a simple human
who can thoughtlessly be around those

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.620
he doesn't get along with.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.120
Matt the hit man...

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.750
In one year, you shall
reincarnate as the first son

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:04.290
of a humble postal worker family
in Halland County of Sweden.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:08.790
I'd rather not live in a cold place.
But who am I to complain?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:13.580
And I didn't think I'd get my second life
arranged showing up for this job.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.950
It is not your second life.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:20.620
This is your 8,740th reincarnation.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.580
That was a really weird sound.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:30.410
Now, Mitsuo, it is your turn to cough up
the karma of this life.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:35.500
Hmm, I'm not too sure
if this counts as karma or not...

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:37.660
But what's always been a mystery to me...

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:43.870
...is that no matter what I do,
I ultimately get girls upset.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.450
Even though I thought I was acting normal,

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:49.290
as you can see, I ended up being murdered today.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:54.250
This is the first time I realized
I had upset her so much.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:58.410
They often say,
"Live honestly with yourself," right?

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.330
But if you really keep on doing
just whatever you want,

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.200
you can hurt others at times, right?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.910
"I've got nothing to do now."
I mean, I know that those words imply

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:10.040
"to the extent that you don't do it
at the expense of others."

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:15.830
But people who don't know what and
how much to tolerate in others exist, too.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:20.160
They say to do unto others as you
would have them do unto you.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.870
But that all depends, and it's
slightly different for each person.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:28.830
I assume there's a huge
discrepancy there in my case.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:33.750
I may be able to apologize to the people who
I've hurt, but I won't be able to feel remorse.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.750
Because I don't actually understand
the fault in my actions.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.330
I'll probably end up doing the same thing again.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:45.500
If I can reincarnate, I want this
discrepancy to be adjusted.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.000
If that's not possible, just let me die here.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.540
Mitsuo... In a year, you shall reincarnate

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:56.870
as a second son of a farmer family
in Blekinge County of Sweden.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.370
Why Sweden?

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.790
They have established welfare there.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.830
Now it's your turn, woman.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:07.250
Cough up the karma of this life.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:11.580
Have you caused any trouble or
done something you deeply regret?

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.580
I'll cleanse it all for you.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.580
"Ad-lib until the end"

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.750
I never asked you to cleanse anything for me.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.500
I killed a man today.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.160
All because of a quarrel
over a mere 500,000 yen.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.540
Do you really think it's right for me
to get that sin cleansed

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.370
and reincarnate into the next life?!

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.290
When you commit murder,
you should account for serving time

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.500
and getting fingers pointed at you
when you're released.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.830
Do I have any regrets?

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:40.910
I have regrets every day,
every hour, and every minute!

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:46.120
Dating a guy who can't differentiate
right from wrong, lending money to him,

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.410
venting about that to a middle-aged man
I just met at a bar!

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:52.080
Getting black-out drunk and
intruding into a stranger's room...

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.040
Saying unnecessary things and
hurting a colleague who likes me!

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:59.660
Responding immaturely to another colleague
who came to admonish me about that!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:03.410
At the quickest, I regret what I've done
within ten seconds after I've done it.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:07.290
But I'm not regretting the fact
that I'm full of regret!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:12.040
I'm not saying that I want to redo
or erase the past, either!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.000
I just want to redeem myself!

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.580
Minare... You will reincarnate
and be sent to Sweden--

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.290
Were you even listening to me?!

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.750
I don't want to live in a place
that's colder than Kushiro!

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:23.410
They don't have Nippon Ham, Taka and Toshi,
or Downtown over there either.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.620
They've got the world's
stinkiest canned product.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.660
Seriously?! Well, that's a different story.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.040
Not! Gosh dammit!

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.950
I don't care about Sweden
or any other foreign country!

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:37.450
I don't care about England
or any other foreign country.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:43.000
Mato, I want your opinion on a
radio program I want to do in Japan.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.370
My throat is damaged...

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:03.160
Yet again, I'm back...

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.200
To being a wandering...

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.870
Send me back to Japan's Aokigahara Sea of Trees!

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.870
Or else I'll kill you!
I don't care if Mt. Fuji blows up!

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:18.120
Until I die... I'm a wandering Japanese!

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.870
Minare Koda!

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:48.000
What I gather from the broadcasts up until now
is that Mr. Kureko really doesn't like me!

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.330
Why do you think that?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.950
Fifty percent of my lines are blank.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.910
The story's forced and it always
ends up being occult-related!

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:58.040
But the listeners love it.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.370
Well, because of its broadcast
gaffe-style content,

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.580
it probably fulfills the listeners'
need for instant gratification.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:04.910
Minare...

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:08.500
What do you think is the most critical technique
for a radio personality to possess?

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:11.450
Huh? Like not stumbling over words
and controlling the volume of your voice,

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.040
something like that?

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.540
Sure, those are things critical
to any voice-related work.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.040
But when it comes to radio personalities...

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.870
The most critical thing is adaptability.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.250
Adaptability?

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.830
For example, let's say something
happens during a live broadcast

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.790
and there's a delay in playing the next song.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:32.120
At that moment do you panic and say, "Oh?
There's something wrong. Please wait a moment."

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.660
Or... "Oh, you know what
that song reminded me of?

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.620
When I was washing my bra
in the bathtub last night..."

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:40.450
Are you able to come up with
a random story like that and fill in the gap?

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:44.620
How adaptable you are defines
your talent as a radio personality.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:49.500
I ordered Kureko to write a script
that can measure your adaptability.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:52.830
Oh... So there was some love
in there, after all!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.080
No, there's no love.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.500
Is that so?!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.790
But, anyway... What did you think
of the Mitsuo I wrote?

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.790
I thought I was able to
recreate him pretty well.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.370
There were some details that felt odd...

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:09.370
But how he starts to shift
into his self-centered reasoning

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:11.790
while he talks about everyday things...

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:15.540
I think you nailed portraying
that loser nature in him.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:16.950
Well, thanks.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:21.290
Well, when I think about it,
it doesn't really matter to the listeners.

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.450
You were able to portray him because
you share that same nature.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.450
Stop that. People will get
the wrong idea about me.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:31.330
Miss Koda, Miss Koda! What did you
think of my Asama-no-Okami?

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.000
Oh, that old hag...

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.370
What? That was you, Miss Chishiro?!

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.290
I was even speaking live, too.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.660
Seriously? From where?!

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.080
At the solo booth usually used
for news broadcasts.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.160
I was listening to your voice from there.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:45.540
Come to think of it, I did get responses
during my ad-lib portions...

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.080
Just so you know, Komoto was
the foundation for Mitsuo's voice.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:48.790
What?!

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.870
They told me my voice was too deep.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.750
What were you thinking, you're an engineer!

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.080
It's not like I had any choice!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.580
Well, I threw a curve ball at Komoto,

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:01.200
and Chishiro seemed bored
since her evening plan was canceled...

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.120
But after all, the reason they agreed to do it

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:09.660
is because they sense something
amazing from you and your program.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.290
I didn't know...

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.200
...that everyone loved me this much...!

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.620
No, it's not love. It's work.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.000
Is that so?!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.330
So, what am I being forced to do next week?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.700
What do you mean, "so"?

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.450
You're going to come up with the next idea.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:34.290
Minare, no matter what kind of program
you want it to be, let me tell you this.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.120
The biggest advantage of radio...

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.790
...is the intimacy with the listeners.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:42.370
Radio-lovers who don't just listen
because their favorite comedian is hosting

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:46.160
are almost always attracted
by the way listeners are treated.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:50.750
As for the broadcasts we've done so far,
although they left a strong impression,

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:54.200
it's actually unconventional that the listeners
have not appeared in the program.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.200
Remember when you barged into
Chishiro's program the first time?

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:02.540
That was a fortunate accident that was able to
happen because it was a live radio broadcast.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.160
Do you want to try to be the one
setting up for those scenarios?

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.370
I could already see myself
eventually getting sued.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:11.200
So, I've been wondering all this time, Minare...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:15.700
Have you even listened to the radio before?
As in voluntarily?

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.080
Oh, actually, well...

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.370
Besides listening to it being played at work,
I've never listened to it at home...

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.700
Ah, I've been listening to
the programs Mizuho listens to.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.160
You don't have a favorite celebrity or anything?

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.080
Besides Taka and Toshi,

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:34.200
I like Shuta Uesugi and Anaguma Taiji.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.700
Well, that's great.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.830
Tonight at midnight, make sure you tune
into HCB's Anaguma-Hunting Prohibited.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:43.620
Experience and see for yourself how much
freedom you have with radio compared to TV.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.620
Okay, I'll give it a listen-- Shoot,
I need to head to the restaurant now.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:50.000
I'll try to come up with an idea, too.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.330
Give me a hot idea that'll
make Mt. Moiwa explode.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:56.290
Way to raise the hurdle.
I'm not a track runner, you know?

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:57.330
Gotta go.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.290
But actually...

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:07.450
Perhaps it works to her advantage
that she doesn't know anything about radio.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:08.790
Morning!

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.040
Sorry I'm a little late.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:13.620
What?! You're apologizing for being late?
Did you catch a cold or something?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:16.040
Nakahara, did you listen to my broadcast?

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.200
I wouldn't miss it.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.660
I listened to it, too.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.950
It was like folklore. I enjoyed it.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.500
Seriously? Even as the personality,
I was thinking,

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.500
"What the hell is going on? Damn radio."

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.450
Well, anyway, it saves time
if you were listening...

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:32.580
As portrayed by that radio drama,
last night, I...

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:34.750
Died and reincarnated!

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:35.410
What?

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:41.410
Therefore, if I was Minare Koda up
until yesterday, from today, I'm...

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.540
...Neo-Minare Koda!

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:46.040
There she goes with her usual nonsense.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.200
Even if it was a topsy-turvy story,

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.750
after I performed it,
it's as if a soul dwelled in those words.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:51.950
Maybe like a placebo effect?

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:56.080
I feel like I'm a totally different
self than before.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.450
If I were to be more specific...

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:03.330
Mitsuo! I can't waste any more time
dragging on about that loser!

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.250
Even though I have a program
with my name in the title,

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.370
my income is still unstable. I have
more important things to think about!

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.620
That said, I'm making a declaration!

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:16.830
I've erased and blocked his number! From now on,
I'll be acting as if he never existed!

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:19.410
She has to declare this to the whole world

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:21.580
because she still has
heavy feelings to get rid of.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:23.540
--I'm gonna go change now.
--Okay.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:28.660
But... Why did she go out of
her way to declare that to me?

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:32.540
I can take it as a declaration that she's
prepared to meet my feelings, right?

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.950
"*Positive-type delusion of reference"
I can take it as a declaration that she's
prepared to meet my feelings, right?

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.160
Oh, yeah, Nakahara, can I have a word with you?

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.620
Ah, by all means!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.660
I'm curious about what you think.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.200
Are you interested in
going on the radio with me?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.330
What?!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.370
With the next broadcast ahead,
Mr. Mato told me this:

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:51.870
"With your talent, it might be pointless for me
to come up with segment ideas every week."

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.250
Are you sure he said it like that?

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:56.500
Well, anyway, there's no time.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.540
So I was wondering if you could
help me out with the first one.

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.000
You could talk about the secret ingredient
you use for the spice mix at the restaurant,

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.040
or a secret menu item that you'll
prepare if you receive an order... Or...

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:09.540
No, never mind! That doesn't sound even
a bit entertaining. Sorry, forget I even asked!

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.830
She just forced me through unnecessary hurt.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.200
You're coming up with ideas
for your radio program?

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:18.290
That's right. Do you have any hot ideas?

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.200
Something that can erupt Mt. Moiwa?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.370
Why don't you ask listeners
to submit some ideas?

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.500
Huh?

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.160
You can launch an open call for ideas
on the official MRS web page

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.750
and on the Twitter account of your program.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:33.450
Wow, Miss Tachibana. How do you know all that?

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:35.870
Oh, I was just curious about it.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:39.330
Then why don't you ask for submissions
on the restaurant's website, too?

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:43.700
No! I appreciate the thought, but remember
why I'm still able to work here.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:48.700
I'm trying to not get fired by helping out
while Manager's at home resting.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:52.580
If I were to use the restaurant's website
like that, all my efforts would be wasted.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:54.580
There'd be no justice on my behalf.

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:57.200
There wasn't any justice in the first place.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.910
Anyway, Miss Minare.
I know I was against it at first,

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:05.580
but since things have come this far,
I'll help you out as much as I can.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.000
I'm always happy to help you out, Miss Minare.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.700
Likewise. If there's anything
I can help with, please let me know.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.700
"Minare"

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:19.200
"Minare"
"You're not alone"

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.910
I know this much.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:32.910
If she's stressed beyond her capacity,
or if something sad happens,

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:36.950
Mizuho starts to sharpen this knife
with intense concentration.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:46.580
She acts cheerful so she
doesn't make me worry,

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.580
but if this continues, this knife
will surpass a Bizen Osafune blade.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.910
Are you okay about the Mr. Kureko thing now?

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:54.830
What?

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.200
Huh? Okay about what?

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:58.500
I know you're forcing yourself to be cheerful

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.250
ever since you heard
Mr. Kureko's quitting radio.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.040
It's painful to watch.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.950
What I'm thinking now...

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:11.450
Is that I hope Mr. Kureko wins
that prize. That's all.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:16.700
Do you really think that, Mizuho?

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:20.040
Don't you want him to lose, deep inside?

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:22.580
Because, when we drank last time...

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:26.000
My goal is to become chief director
within two years of today!

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:29.620
With you, Minare Koda as the main DJ and
Katsumi Kureko as the broadcast writer,

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.660
my unprecedented dream team,

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:36.080
I'll convince the producers to let me
direct a three-hour long block!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.750
That was her dream... This is too sad.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.660
I want to pat her back so badly.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.620
--Maybe I'll steal a kiss, too...
--Miss Minare.

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:43.700
Huh?

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:48.250
Does this mean she's all prepared for it?

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:51.950
But when it comes down to it, I don't know
if I have the guts to kiss her...

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.830
Weren't you going to listen
to the radio tonight?

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:55.660
What?

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:58.370
Ah! You're right!

00:20:58.370 --> 00:21:01.160
Good evening! It's time for
Anaguma-Hunting Prohibited!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.910
Hosted by Taizo Anaguma,
the minister of gout and...!

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:06.500
Jiro Anaguma, the prince of the chronic hernia.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.080
All right! As advertised, this week's broadcast,

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:11.120
just like last time,
is produced by Joker Skonsky!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.450
If Joker's content gets used next time,
they'll show up in our studio!

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.540
Let's hope they're a high-school girl!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.950
Without further ado, let's get started!
This one's titled, "Superb Song."

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:21.750
--Eriko! I'll turn my feelings for you
into a song tonight!

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:25.040
--This Joker Skonsky person is on a roll.
--Eriko! I'll turn my feelings for you
into a song tonight!

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:27.160
--They've got an obscure sense of style.
--♬ I remember the first thing you told me
when I met you at the autumn beach. ♬

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.370
--I'm sure they'll be invited
to the studio eventually.
--♬ I remember the first thing you told me
when I met you at the autumn beach. ♬

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:35.250
--"Let us know what you want to hear on
the radio, we'll make it happen" kinda thing?
--♬ I remember the first thing you told me
when I met you at the autumn beach. ♬

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:39.500
--You could also say that they're attempting
to foster broadcast writers.
--♬ "Your profile looks like
Chiba prefecture." ♬

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:40.410
--I wonder if Mr. Mato wants me
to do my program like this.
--♬ "Your profile looks like
Chiba prefecture." ♬

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:43.620
--I wonder if Mr. Mato wants me
to do my program like this.
--It's too long!
--Please let me sing it all the way through!

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:44.750
--Oh, I'd love to listen to that!
--I only have 155 more verses to go!

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:46.870
--Oh, I'd love to listen to that!
--Is this the Greek national anthem?!

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.830
--But... how can I put this?
--You've changed... You never used to judge
others by the color of their skin like that.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:49.950
--I have a feeling Mr. Mato isn't expecting
radio like this from you at all.
--You've changed... You never used to judge
others by the color of their skin like that.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:55.620
--I have a feeling Mr. Mato isn't expecting
radio like this from you at all.
--I'm talking about your clothes! Why the heck are
you wearing clothes with colors like Lush soap?!

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:59.580
--To say that it's "new" might
sound appealing, but actually...
--If I were to respond to you by song...

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.410
I think he wants something more...

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:06.160
...wild living in the moment and anarchistic,
something like that.

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:11.500
Whoa, Mizuho. How could you say
something so bold with a straight face?

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:30.410
"Next Episode"

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:32.870
"Preview"
What will happen to my feelings for Mr. Kureko?

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:35.160
"Preview"
My feelings for my book?

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:37.540
"Preview"
My feelings for Mr. Nakahara?

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:39.910
My feelings for my younger sister?

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:42.040
My feelings for Miss Minare?!

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:44.080
My feelings for radio?

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:46.200
My feelings for Mitsuo-- No!

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:48.200
My feelings for becoming a DJ?!

00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:50.790
My feelings for Mr. Toru--

00:23:50.790 --> 00:23:53.160
Everyone's feelings cross in the final episode!

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:58.950
<i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:
"I Want to Convey It to You."

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.910
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
